; Root environment: variables shared across packages, plus the root scripts, migrations and tests.
;
; Package-only settings live in that package's template: backend ones (Auth0 M2M, Cloudinary,
; Hive, Anthropic, Google Drive, OpenTelemetry, log levels, …) in packages/server/.env.template,
; client ones (AUTH0_FRONTEND_CLIENT_ID, GRAPHQL_URL, DEV_AUTH_USER_ID) in
; packages/client/.env.template, bank-scraper dev credentials in
; packages/modern-poalim-scraper/.env.template. The server, the client and those dev scripts fall
; back to this file for anything their own .env does not set, so whatever is set here reaches them
; too. (mcp-server, the email-ingestion gateway and the crypto scrapers read only their own .env.)
;
; Conventions: active entries are required for local development; commented-out `# VAR=value`
; entries are optional. `scripts/__tests__/env-templates.test.ts` fails on an entry nothing reads.

############
# Database #
############

; KEEP THESE POINTED AT THE LOCAL DEV CONTAINER. This file is read by codegen, migrations,
; seeds and every DB-backed test, so whatever is set here is what `yarn test`, `yarn
; generate` and `migration:run` all target -- including `vitest --project unit`, whose
; global setup writes reference data before any test runs.
;
; Credentials for a deployed database belong in a separate, explicitly named file (e.g.
; .env.production, also git-ignored) that you pass deliberately -- never here.
;
; Guard behaviour is not uniform, so do not rely on it as a blanket block
; (packages/migrations/src/local-db-guard.ts):
;   - tests, the vitest global setup and the seed scripts REFUSE a non-local host outright,
;     unless you opt in for that one command with ALLOW_REMOTE_DB=1
;   - `migration:run` only WARNS and then proceeds, because production deploys may apply
;     migrations during the build; set ENFORCE_LOCAL_DB=1 to make it refuse too
;   - codegen (`yarn generate` / pgTyped) is NOT guarded at all -- it only reads, so it will
;     silently introspect whatever host is set here
;
; Shared with the server. `1` connects over SSL (default: 0).
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_DB=accounter
POSTGRES_SSL='0'

; Schema the DB-backed tests and `scripts/verify-migrations.ts` inspect (default: accounter_schema).
# POSTGRES_SCHEMA=accounter_schema

; Recommended: set this in your shell profile so `migration:run` refuses a non-local host
; outright instead of only warning.
# ENFORCE_LOCAL_DB=1

; Per-command opt-in, never set in this file: `ALLOW_REMOTE_DB=1 <command>` lets tests and seeds
; run against a non-local host for that one command.
# ALLOW_REMOTE_DB=1

#########
# Seeds #
#########

; `yarn seed:production` (scripts/seed.ts): accounts to create for the admin business. Add more
; with a numeric suffix (SEED_BANK_ACCOUNT_NUMBER_2, SEED_BANK_NUMBER_2, SEED_BRANCH_NUMBER_2,
; SEED_CREDIT_CARD_LAST4DIGITS_2, …); the first missing one ends the list.
# SEED_BANK_ACCOUNT_NUMBER=1234567890
# SEED_BANK_NUMBER=12
# SEED_BRANCH_NUMBER=123
# SEED_CREDIT_CARD_LAST4DIGITS=1234
; Comma-separated currencies: each seeded account gets a tax category per currency.
# SEED_CURRENCIES=USD,ILS

; Demo seed (`yarn seed:staging-demo`, scripts/seed-demo-data.ts). Per-command opt-in, never set in
; this file: the script refuses to run without `ALLOW_DEMO_SEED=1`, or with NODE_ENV=production.
# ALLOW_DEMO_SEED=1
; Optional Auth0 user id to link to the seeded demo admin user. Leave unset to seed it without an
; Auth0 identity.
# DEMO_AUTH0_USER_ID=

########
# Auth #
########

; Auth0 tenant domain (bare hostname) and API audience. Shared: the server verifies tokens with
; them and the client requests tokens for them.
AUTH0_DOMAIN=your-tenant.us.auth0.com
AUTH0_AUDIENCE=https://api.accounter.com

; Local development only: `1` lets the client send, and the server accept, an
; `X-Dev-Auth: <user-id>` header instead of an Auth0 login. Must be `1` or `0` (the server refuses
; to start otherwise). Never set in a deployed environment. Pick the user with DEV_AUTH_USER_ID
; (see packages/client/.env.template).
# ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=1

#######################
# Tooling and runtime #
#######################

; `yarn migration:check-conflicts` (scripts/check-migration-conflicts.ts). `1` only warns on
; conflicts, `0` (the default) fails. The refs default to origin/main and HEAD.
# MIGRATION_CONFLICT_WARN_ONLY=0
# MIGRATION_CONFLICT_BASE_REF=origin/main
# MIGRATION_CONFLICT_HEAD_REF=HEAD

; Local development only (richer library logs). Never set in production: libraries key their debug
; output off DEBUG, and some of it includes request headers and bodies. Server and Green Invoice
; logs ignore it; use SERVER_LOG_LEVEL and GREEN_INVOICE_LOG_LEVEL (see packages/server/.env.template).
; `DEBUG=accounter:test` turns on the server test-harness diagnostics.
DEBUG=1

; Leave unset locally. Every package that falls back to this file inherits it: `production` makes
; the demo seed refuse to run and switches the server to production behaviour (masked errors,
; OTEL_DEPLOYMENT_ENV). Deployed environments set it themselves.
# NODE_ENV=development

; Any non-empty value silences dotenv's debug output in the server and in migrations (which, when it
; is unset, also loads packages/migrations/.env). Meant for deployed environments.
# RELEASE=1
